WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.980
Can they escape from the underground cell?

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.650
The new teacher at DDS, Hongou-sensei,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.910
ordered Kyuu and I to clean the old school building.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.530
While cleaning the documents room,

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.700
we found a room that wasn't on the plans for this building.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.040
Entranced by the riddles in Front of him,

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:50.250
Kyuu used his natural persistence and at last opened the door,

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.760
and we entered the pitch-black basement.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:02:00.010
But at that time somebody was already plotting to get us.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.110
That's a pit viper!

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:13.940
Dammit!

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:30.670
Kyuu...

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:31.880
Megu.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:32.880
Are you OK?

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.550
What should we do, Kyuu?

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.720
It looks like I was bitten.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.680
What should I do?

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:49.190
If you're bitten by a pit viper you die within hours
unless you get an injection of antivenom.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.520
We're already in grave danger just being down here.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.320
We're done for.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.780
We're done for!

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.570
Calm down Megu.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.030
Show me your leg.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.340
OK, I've sucked out all I can.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.890
But now we're sure.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.680
There are no pit vipers on Honshuu, and especially not in Tokyo.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.350
That means that...

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:39.780
Yeah, whoever locked us in here also put that
pit viper in here through that opening...

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.700
to kill us.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.330
It's Fine, Megu.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.460
We're in the Q-Class in DDS.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.050
Let's think of a way out.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.760
No matter how desperate things may get, you can't give up until the end.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:06.760
Right?

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.430
So let's do our best, Megu!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.270
What?

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.650
Kyuu and Megu aren't home yet?

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:24.070
Yeah, when I got done with my job and went
to Kyuu's place his mom was in a panic.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.660
I've got a bad feeling... and in situations like this it's 100 percent right.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.500
But you don't think they're off having fun on their own or something?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.040
Idiot.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.670
You're too young to be saying that!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.880
It is true, that based on Megu's personality,

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:45.390
it's quite possible she stayed behind to help Kyuu with the cleaning.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:51.230
But even if cleaning the old building takes a while, it shouldn't take this long.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:57.270
Kyuu might not, but if Megu were going to be late she would call home.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.650
Dammit... anyway let's head back to DDS.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.070
There might be something in the old building.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:08.990
Hey, you guys.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.830
Ouda-san, Shishidou-san.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.370
Sorry, we're in a hurry.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.290
Did something happen?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.340
Would you come with us?

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.010
The lights are off.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.230
And the cleaning supplies have all been put away.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.360
Their bags are gone from the room...

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.490
think they might've gone home after all?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.120
No, they didn't.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:55.750
This bucket... the insides are still wet and it's obviously been filled with water.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.880
But the towels and mops are still dry.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:05.010
lf they were going to just sweep and clean up, they wouldn't fill the bucket.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.840
Then what...

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.800
In other words, after the two of them finished sweeping...

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.520
and before they started mopping, there was some kind of accident.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.270
Wait... then who put away the cleaning supplies?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.610
Somebody else, then.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.400
You can't mean that they were kidnapped, like Yukigawa-san?

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.780
No way!

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:31.280
For someone to walk out with a pair of kidnapped students...

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:32.950
the academy's security isn't loose enough for that.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.960
Does that mean that they've disappeared somewhere inside the school?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.380
Dammit, isn't there some kind of definite clue?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.090
Right! Their bags!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.340
DDS handbook rule 21.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.470
"Start looking for evidence in the trash.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.270
Are you OK, Megu.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.850
lt just hurts a bit.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.190
Stay as still as possible.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.810
That should make it harder for the poison to circulate.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.910
Why was that diary burned?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.740
Probably the person in here made it out.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.960
‘Cause if they died down here,

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.330
the person who came to get rid of the body wouldn't
go through all the trouble of burning it.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:24.920
They burned it when they escaped

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.090
That s why they couldn't tell that it wasn't completely destroyed.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.930
But how did they get out of this basement?

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:32.720
A hole out or something?

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.890
No, that's impossible.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:40.140
Judging from that iron door and that small opening for food,

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.810
this whole basement was built to lock somebody in.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.690
You'd never make a hole in a prison cell.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.070
That means...

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:54.490
they used some trick to deceive the person
who locked them in and then escaped!

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.750
There might be some clue in their diary...

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.500
Bingo, Kyuu.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:04.920
Those are Megu and Kyuu's bags.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:09.840
lt seems clear that somebody's up to something.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:10.920
Huh?

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.390
What's this stainless steel can thing?

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:17.970
A hole?

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.640
This smells bad.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.060
Hey, lemme see that.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.400
What's that?

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:26.900
It's not the DDS Notebook.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.110
This is an original detective tool that I made.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.160
I based it off the DDS Notebook.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:38.910
There are a ton of great tools in here that
even the DDS notebook doesn't have!

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.580
Stop bragging and start checking!

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:46.250
It looks like they hid some kind of animal in the bottom.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:49.760
These holes in the bottom are air-holes.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.220
Animal? What kind of animal?

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.800
Wait a second, there's still something left on the bottom.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:55.590
A scale!

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:56.930
A fish or something?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.220
If it was a Fish they wouldn't use air holes.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.310
It's gotta be some kind of reptile

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.060
Reptile?

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:08.520
I'll look at the scale's pattern with a microscope
and photograph it with my digital camera.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:15.030
OK... if I match this picture with my database of reptiles...

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:17.410
Found it!

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:18.660
This is a Habu!

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.830
It's the scale of the Habu pit viper, a poisonous snake from Okinawa!

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:26.710
Kazuma! What's the closest hospital with a sample of Habu antivenom?

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.840
Umm... wait a second.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:32.090
The lab at Tokyo Imperial University Hospital probably has some.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:33.630
Kinta!

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.970
All right, leave it to me!

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.470
Go get some Habu antivenom just in case, right?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.600
If I use one of the academy's motorcycles I can have it here in 30 minutes.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.310
I'm counting on you, Kinta.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:45.770
What a group...

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.110
The reason all this happened is because I made Kyuu do my cleaning!

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.530
Please, let me be in time... Kyuu, Megu!

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.950
lf Kyuu and Megu haven't left the academy grounds...

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.250
they must be locked up somewhere.

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:07.620
But where?

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.260
All we can make out is the date and the first few lines.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:19.140
Look, up until here it's got a record of what Food
was given to him and that he ate it, but...

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:25.180
after here, the entry only records the menu, and
and only says he ate it on every other day...

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:26.600
What's that mean?

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.190
Maybe he just felt like it?

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:31.070
No, there must be some reason.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:34.860
this is strange.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.450
Let's try to think like the person who was locked in here.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.620
Let's assume this was the hard bread...

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.290
and the day that he didn't say whether he ate it...

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.040
let's assume he didn't, I guess.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:47.960
Didn't.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:49.630
Didn't.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.050
I get it!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:57.800
If you eat one day's food over two days,

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.340
then over 10 days you'll still have five days worth.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:04.100
I understand how he got out of here.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:10.480
In other words whoever was in here ate his food little by little,

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:16.490
then one day he just stopped taking the food
that was offered through the opening.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.900
He kept quiet and ate the food he'd saved up, and pretended to be dead.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.660
After one or two weeks,

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:26.290
the people who locked him in here would surely assume that he was dead.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:30.460
Then they'd come in to get rid of the body and...

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:41.260
But if they really got out that way, we can't.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.430
Hang on, Megu!

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.020
Water.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:50.350
Give me water.

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:50.850
Water...

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.360
there's no water here.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.150
Water!

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:58.490
He had nothing to save that much water in.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:02.610
But you can't live weeks without water.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:05.450
In other words, you can get water from somewhere in here.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:09.910
There wouldn't be a spring or anything here in the city...

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.000
maybe there's a place where water drips in here.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.880
It might be a hint to help us get out of here.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:22.930
Think.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:25.800
It Kyuu and Megu were bitten by a sake...

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:27.180
they can’t waste time.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.640
Yes... if I were Kyuu,

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:33.190
I wouldn't give up, I'd keep thinking of a way to get out.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.570
It was Kuzuryuu Takumi who built this?

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.320
Dammit, I can't fall asleep at a time like this...

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.580
I'm gonna wash my face and try to wake up.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:51.960
Amakusa, don't you think there's no point in looking here Further?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.750
We've looked everywhere we can...

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:56.500
shouldn't we try the new building?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:57.960
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:00.760
Ryuu-kun! Come here.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.380
Kazuma, did you Find something?

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.680
What s up, elementary schooler?

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:06.600
Look at this!

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:07.970
This is...

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:11.430
It's Flashing...

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.020
The water Faucet is Flashing!

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.480
It's Kyuu... that's an SOS signal from Kyuu!

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:24.990
It's Flashing!

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:26.410
The water Faucet is Flashing.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:28.860
It's making a small sound too!

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:33.080
This Flash... isn't it the Flashlight from the DDS notebook?

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:34.410
It's Kyuu.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.500
It's an SOS from Kyuu!

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:40.750
The water pressure has gone down ..

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:43.170
somebody's opened a faucet!

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.130
Notice, please!

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.840
Amazing, Kyuu...

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.760
when he started banging at the ceiling water pipes with a knife...

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:58.690
and the stone he found I thought he was nuts,

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:03.190
but maybe, just maybe we'll be saved now.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.820
It's gotta’ be the DDS notebook Flashlight!

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.950
They can't be that far!

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:12.820
Yeah.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.410
Wait... what do you mean?

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.750
It's the same principle used in optic fiber.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:22.420
You've seen falling water shine in Fountains and stuff right?

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.710
In those Fountains the light source is inside the Fountain...

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:28.840
and the Flowing water bends and carries the light.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.930
In the same way, somewhere this water pipe's got a hole in it,

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:34.800
and from there Kyuu and Megu are sending the light signal.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.390
Water pipes... that would mean they're underground!

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:42.770
But there aren't any entrances leading down in this building.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:45.150
Ryuo-kun...

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:50.240
Ryuu-kun?

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:52.950
That shelf...

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.160
What about the shelf?

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.160
It's been moved.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.330
OK, let's move it!

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:10.510
There's a room beyond this...

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.720
What is this door?

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:18.850
Nine dragons.

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:21.430
Nine?

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.770
There are 10...

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:28.150
The map we saw said it was Kuzuryuu Takumi who built this place, right?

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:29.650
Yeah...

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.780
Kuzuryuu, in other words nine dragons.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.280
There are 10 here.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:37.530
One too many.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:38.790
But...

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.920
one's gone and now there are nine!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:49.710
It's open.

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:51.550
A staircase leading down.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.260
All right.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:57.140
I'm sorry... could you two stay here on guard?

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:58.810
But...

00:15:59.040 --> 00:15:59.760
Please.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.270
Let's go, Kazuma.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.020
Right.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.860
Ryuu-kun, why did you leave them up there?

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.610
One of them might've been the one who locked them in.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:15.490
If that's true then leaving only one is dangerous.

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:19.200
No way... those two are A-class DDS members.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.620
There's no way they'd do that.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.290
If it's really them.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.340
Kyuu, Megu, where are you?

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.220
Are you OK?

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:37.090
Kyuu!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:38.970
Megu's in danger!

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:39.720
Hurry!

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.060
It's OK.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:45.190
Kinta has gone to get the antivenom.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:45.810
He'll be here right away.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:46.690
Hey!

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:49.560
I'm back and I got the Antivenom!

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:51.440
I'm so glad.

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:52.940
I'm so glad...

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:55.570
if something happened to Megu...

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.450
Hey!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.590
None of the security cameras show anyone suspicious.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:13.550
Which means that, as we suspected...

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:21.180
The person who locked them in there and tried
to kill them didn't come from outside.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.310
Or at least look like it.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:25.810
What do you think, Maki-kun?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.850
I think that's quite possible.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.230
There are presently 87 students in this school,

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:36.950
twelve were here late the night of the incident.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:38.950
One of them...

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:42.120
It's also possible that a member of Pluto disguised themselves.

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:46.540
Dan-sensei, let's check all the students

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:47.960
Hongou-kun...

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.880
If nothing else we need to check the 20 who were there that night,

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:57.590
including a physical to look for the Crest of Pluto.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.010
You're an idiot, Hongou.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:00.970
What?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:05.140
You think a mere physical would reveal their Crest?

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:09.190
They've hidden their crests with a special water-resistant makeup.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.310
The same with their disguise...

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.190
there's even a possibility of plastic surgery!

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:17.320
If you want to find them,

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:21.240
you'd better be prepared to rip the skin off the face of every single student.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.040
Then let's hear your idea, Nagami.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:29.870
Or are we just going to sit back and wait for one of the students to get killed?

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:31.830
That's not my intention.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:33.250
Dan-sensei...

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.250
Let me investigate.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:39.970
I'll interview them one by one, and using my deductive skills, I'll-

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:42.050
You're the idiot.

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:45.760
Their acting is far superior to their make-up.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:50.940
With your intuition dulled by sitting around here
at DDS do you really think you could find them?

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.480
I don't want to hear that from somebody who ended up here...

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:57.530
after screwing up on the job and spending a month in the hospital.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:59.440
What did you say?

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:00.240
Stop it, both of you.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.280
I'll handle this for now.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:11.040
Focus on improving the school's security.

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:12.000
Yes!

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:16.590
Who was locked inside that underground cell,

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:22.590
who was this mysterious Kuzuryuu Takumi who built the building,

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.890
and what about that murder that happened there?

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:27.720
There are still things unsolved in this matter.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:33.770
I would love to investigate myself, but with this body...

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:37.230
I must rely on you

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:39.820
Leave it to me, Dan-sensei!

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.400
OF course!

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.030
Anything you want!

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:46.410
Let's get all the old murder data we have together.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.910
Where should we start, sensei?

00:19:50.730 --> 00:19:52.080
Then let us begin.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.130
DDS is temporarily closed?

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.710
The teachers are all looked really strange and went off to hold a confrence.

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:02.760
I didn't think it'd get this big.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.050
You're awful calm about it.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:07.220
It's your fault isn't it?

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.100
And thanks to you Megu almost died.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:15.980
Huh? Didn't this all happen because you made Kyuu do your cleaning?

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.360
You didn't need to bring that up again!

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:22.690
But that door was a surprising discovery.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:28.120
Megu and Kyuu solved a mystery that even Dan-sensei didn't find.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.910
In a way, isn't that rewarding?

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:34.870
But why was that underground cell built?

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:39.130
And who was locked-up in there?

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:44.010
And what about that murder that supposedly occurred there?

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.260
They're probably linked.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.140
Kuzuryu Takumi.

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:52.850
He s the one who designed that building.

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.190
Maybe if we investigate it...

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.440
I tried that, but...

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:00.150
No matter which database I check...

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:01.610
Kuzuryuu Takumi.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:04.440
Death, unknown.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:13.040
Architect, sculptor, composer, poet. A man of many
talents, also called the all-around genius.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:17.670
He is also said to be one of the pioneers of trick art in Japan...

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:21.170
but very little information exists as to his personal history,

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:27.930
and all that remains are the works thought to be his.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.430
What?

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:32.890
Your  net data you're so proud of isn't that useful at all, is it?

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:38.520
Old data like this is better found in libraries than on the net.

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:42.650
A mansion built by a pioneer of trick art.

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:46.320
A mysterious person sealed in a secret cellar.

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:52.580
There may be more mysteries hidden in that building.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.700
Oh, it's time for my job.

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:57.250
Megu, take care of yourself.

00:21:58.270 --> 00:21:59.250
I'm going home too.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.000
See you at school.

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.630
Kyuu... Kyuu will you stay with me?

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:18.390
It's bothering me. Who tried to kill us?

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:27.650
If we don't know who did it, they may come after us again, and next time...

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:29.070
I'm sorry, Meguu.

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:35.990
If I'd listen to you when you said not to go in, and gone to get somebody...

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:38.790
we never would've been locked in and I never would've put you in danger.

00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:40.370
I'm really sorry.

00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:42.380
It's OK, Kyuu!

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:44.880
It's not only your Fault.

00:22:45.570 --> 00:22:47.590
I was careless too, and...

00:22:48.030 --> 00:22:50.930
well if we break down over something like this,

00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:52.840
we'll never make it as detectives will we?

00:22:53.410 --> 00:22:54.890
So don't worry about it.

00:22:59.120 --> 00:22:59.730
I'm home.

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:02.440
Welcome home, Kyuu-sama.

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:05.110
There s something I'd like to ask you.

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:06.520
What is this?

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:12.280
Two of the members of DDS's Q-Class were almost killed by someone.

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.530
Do you have some kind of idea, Irui-san?

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:17.740
No, I'm sorry I don't.

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:21.120
Let me say this.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:26.670
I'm going to DDS because of my grandfather's direct order.

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:28.840
I won't allow any selfish actions.

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:31.760
Understood, Ryuu-sama.

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:41.010
Continues!

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.270 --> 00:24:48.670
An evil that lurks on the web.

00:24:47.440 --> 00:24:56.300
Next Episode

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:50.630
Terror From an invisible world.

00:24:51.270 --> 00:24:53.670
A missing persons incident at a famous high school

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:55.550
Rumors of a video showing the murder.

00:24:56.150 --> 00:24:59.390
Ryuu and Megu receive an order to sneak in and investigate from DDS.

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:05.600
Who will be the star of the next video that the murderous collector shoots?

00:25:08.830 --> 00:25:10.100
If that was Ryuu-kun...

00:25:15.050 --> 00:25:19.240
I shouldn't, really, I really shouldn't think about that. Huh...
